# Multiple farms and enterprises

A farmer can own or operate more than one farm. Each farm can run more than one enterprise.

- Do not model a farmer as a single farm or a single sector.
- Persist farms as a list. Persist enterprises against a specific `farmId`.
- After saving a farm or finishing an enterprise, return to a holdings list so the agent can add another farm or another enterprise.
- Sector forms stay unique to the chain, and are scoped to that farm × enterprise pair.
